# Scratch work, not the project.
#
# Everything here is a THROWAWAY: one-shot probes written to answer one
# question, mutation tables written to prove the suite bites, and their
# captured output. They are kept rather than deleted because re-proving a
# check next time is cheaper than rewriting the table that proves it — but
# they are not part of the build, nobody should have to read them, and they
# must never reach a commit.
#
# The convention is the leading underscore, and it is the whole rule: a file
# named _anything is scratch. Everything without one is the project.
#
# NOT ignored, and deliberately so:
#   scripts/test-engine.mjs   the suite itself
#   scripts/domshim.mjs       the DOM the suite renders into, headless
#   scripts/peershim.mjs      the transport the suite talks over, headless
#   scripts/gen-icons.js      generates icons/, which ships
_*

# ...but the shipped page is index.html, and no underscore file is loaded by
# it. If that ever stops being true, this pattern is the thing that hides it.

# Editor/session state. .claude/ holds per-machine launch settings and
# transcripts, neither of which belong to anybody else checking this out.
.claude/

# OS and editor litter.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# There are no dependencies — package.json has no "dependencies" key and the
# page loads ES modules straight from js/. node_modules/ should never appear;
# it is listed so that if some tool creates one, it does not get committed by
# somebody who did not notice.
node_modules/
